  23: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  24:     """
  25:     Recolor the object whose shape matches the colored template inside the grey L-frame.
  26: 
  27:     Input structure:
  28:     - The black background contains one grey L-frame, with its vertical leg on
  29:       the right and horizontal leg on the bottom of the frame bbox.
  30:     - A single colored template object lies in the area enclosed above-left by
  31:       that L-frame.
  32:     - Other colored objects are scattered outside the framed template region.
  33: 
  34:     Rule:
  35:     - Extract the normalized mask of the colored template inside the grey
  36:       L-frame bbox.
  37:     - Find the unique outside object with the same normalized mask, ignoring
  38:       its color.
  39:     - Recolor that matched outside object to grey and leave all other pixels
  40:       unchanged.
  41: 
  42:     Key insight:
  43:     The grey L-frame is a shape selector: it marks the template to search for
  44:     elsewhere in the scene.
  45:     """
